.TH scene-preview 1 "AUGUST 2026" Linux "User Manuals"
.SH NAME
scene-preview \- non-locking SVG scene-v1 preview and inspection utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scene-preview
.BI --scene " scene.svg"
.BI --size " WIDTHxHEIGHT"
[\fB--output\fR \fIframe.png\fR]
[\fB--inspect\fR]
[\fB--window\fR [\fB--watch\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scene-preview
renders, inspects, benchmarks, and live-previews i3lock-svg-nh scene-v1 SVGs
without invoking PAM, grabbing input, or creating a lock window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --scene " PATH"
Load an already packed, runtime-safe scene SVG.
.TP
.BI --source " PATH"
Load an editable authoring SVG by packing linked local PNGs in memory first.
The runtime loader remains strict; this option is for preview only.
.TP
.BI --size " WIDTHxHEIGHT"
Set the target render size.
.TP
.BI --state " locked|input|verify|fail"
Set the active state for a still frame, sequence, benchmark, or live preview.
.TP
.BI --initial-state " locked|input|verify|fail"
Set the simulated startup state before a scheduled state transition.
.TP
.BI --state-at-ms " N"
Apply
.B --state
at absolute simulated time
.IR N .
.TP
.BI --trigger " key|backspace"
Fire a one-shot trigger for a still-frame preview.
.TP
.BI --trigger-at-ms " N"
Apply
.B --trigger
at absolute simulated time
.IR N .
.TP
.BI --time-ms " N"
Render a still frame at absolute simulated time
.IR N .
.TP
.BI --output " PATH"
Write a still-frame PNG.
.TP
.BI --window
Open a normal decorated X11 preview window. This is not a locker.
.TP
.BI --watch
Watch the source SVG and linked PNG dependencies and reload transactionally.
.TP
.BI --fullscreen
Request fullscreen preview-window state without grabbing input.
.TP
.BI --no-overlay
Disable the preview-only diagnostics overlay.
.TP
.BI --reload-error-to-stderr
Print live-reload failures to standard error while retaining the last valid frame.
.TP
.BI --screenshot-dir " PATH"
Directory for live-preview screenshots written with the
.B S
key.
.TP
.BI --inspect
Print the retained cache layout and memory accounting.
.TP
.BI --inspect-json " PATH"
Write deterministic inspection JSON.
.TP
.BI --duration-ms " N"
Render a deterministic sequence for
.I N
simulated milliseconds.
.TP
.BI --fps " N"
Set sequence frame rate.
.TP
.BI --output-dir " PATH"
Write sequence PNG frames and a JSON manifest to this directory.
.TP
.BI --state-change " TIME:STATE"
Schedule a state change in sequence mode. May be supplied multiple times.
.TP
.BI --trigger-event " TIME:TRIGGER"
Schedule a one-shot trigger in sequence mode. May be supplied multiple times.
.TP
.BI --contact-sheet " PATH"
Write a PNG contact sheet for rendered sequence frames.
.TP
.BI --contact-columns " N"
Set contact-sheet columns.
.TP
.BI --contact-every " N"
Use every Nth rendered frame in the contact sheet.
.TP
.BI --benchmark
Benchmark bounded and full-target reference cache modes.
.TP
.BI --benchmark-frames " N"
Set measured benchmark frame count.
.TP
.BI --benchmark-fps " N"
Set simulated benchmark frame rate.
.TP
.BI --benchmark-warmup-frames " N"
Set warmup frames excluded from benchmark percentiles.
.TP
.BI --benchmark-json " PATH"
Write deterministic benchmark JSON, excluding timing values from reproducibility guarantees.
.TP
.BI --version
Print the build version.
.TP
.BI --help
Print usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR i3lock (1),
.BR scene-pack (1)
